    "body": "### Description\nFollowing up on the token generation (Phase 1) #40820, this issue covers **Phases 2 & 3** of the token authentication plan: Channel State Management and RPC Enforcement.\n\nCurrently, any client that can route to a Neovim TCP socket can execute arbitrary msgpack-RPC commands. We need to introduce an \"Authenticate-First\" policy.\n\n**Proposed Changes:**\n1. Introduce a `bool is_authenticated` flag to the `Channel` struct (`src/nvim/channel.h`).\n2. Initialize this flag to `false` for `UV_TCP` channels, and `true` for Unix sockets/Stdio (`src/nvim/channel.c`).\n3. Intercept incoming RPC calls (`src/nvim/msgpack_rpc/channel.c`). If the channel is unauthenticated, the *only* permitted method is a new API call: `nvim_authenticate(String token)`.\n4. If an unauthenticated client requests any other method, drop the connection immediately (`channel_close()`) to prevent enumeration or SSRF attacks.\n5. Use a constant-time string comparison for the token check to prevent timing attacks.\n\n### State Machine\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[Client connects via TCP] --> B{is_auth?}\n    B -- True --> C[Process RPC normally]\n    B -- False --> D{Method == auth?}\n    D -- Yes --> C\n    D -- No --> E[Drop Connection]\n```\n<!-- Attach issue2.gif from CS/scratch/ here -->\n",
